0. Terminology

  0.1. "The Pack" means the software package in which this exact license
       file is found, including all shader sources, scripts, tools,
       documentation, generated images and configuration files contained
       in it. A Fork is not "The Pack" for the purposes of this license.

  0.2. "Normal Usage" means using The Pack as intended for the general
       public. This includes, but is not limited to:

       a. Loading The Pack in Minecraft: Java Edition to play the game,
          including on multiplayer servers and on servers that sell ranks,
          subscriptions or other perks to their players.

       b. Recording, streaming, screenshotting and rendering with The Pack,
          and publishing or monetizing the resulting content.

       c. Making cinematic works, films, music videos or other audiovisual
          works with The Pack.

       d. Modifying The Pack for personal use without publishing it.

  0.3. "User" and "Users" means any person who accesses, uses or
       distributes The Pack, including under sections 1.3, 1.4 and 1.5.

  0.4. "Modpack" means a modification package made for the video game
       "Minecraft: Java Edition" that bundles multiple independent pieces
       of content.

  0.5. "Fork" means a software package that contains code from The Pack
       and in which that code has been intentionally changed to differ
       from The Pack.

  0.6. "Original Pack" means the pack named "Ray" published by kuwacom.

  0.7. "Official Distribution Channels" means repositories and download
       pages published by kuwacom, including the GitHub repository at
       https://github.com/kuwacom/ray, and any Modrinth or CurseForge
       project page that kuwacom controls.

1. Grants

  1.1. All Users are free to use The Pack for Normal Usage. No payment,
       attribution or permission is required for Normal Usage.

  1.2. Content created with The Pack, including videos, streams,
       screenshots, films and renders, is the work of the person who
       created it. kuwacom makes no claim of ownership over such content,
       whether or not it is monetized. Credit is appreciated but not
       required.

  1.3. The Pack may be included in a Modpack, including a Modpack that is
       sold or otherwise monetized, as long as the following conditions
       are met:

       a. The Modpack has substantial content of its own. A Modpack whose
          primary purpose is to distribute The Pack, or which contains
          little besides The Pack, does not qualify.

       b. The Pack must be visibly credited, with a link to an Official
          Distribution Channel, in the Modpack's description page(s),
          whether or not The Pack is enabled by default for new users.

       c. The copy of The Pack placed in the Modpack must be complete and
          unmodified, including this license file. Changing option defaults,
          changing block properties or adding content to The Pack itself does
          not satisfy this condition.

       Support is provided for The Pack as published by kuwacom only.
       Problems caused by a Modpack, or by changes made to The Pack inside
       one, are not covered.

  1.4. A Fork may be published as long as the following conditions are met:

       a. The Fork must visibly credit the Original Pack as "Based on Ray
          by kuwacom", including a link to an Official Distribution
          Channel. This credit must appear in the first paragraph of the
          Fork's description page(s) and in the first paragraph of the
          Fork's README or equivalent documentation. Burying the credit
          at the end of a long description does not satisfy this
          condition.

       b. The Fork must not be named in a way that could reasonably be
          mistaken for the Original Pack or for an official product of
          kuwacom. Using "Ray" as the whole name, or in a variant that
          suggests an official continuation (for example "Ray 2",
          "Ray Reimagined", "Ray RT"), is not allowed. The word "Ray" may
          only be used descriptively, to state that the Fork is based on
          Ray. The same applies to domain names, social media handles,
          repository names and store page titles.

       c. The Fork must not use the name, logo, avatars or other identity
          of kuwacom, or of the Original Pack, in a way that presents them
          as belonging to the Fork or as an endorsement of the Fork.

       d. The Fork must differ substantively from the Original Pack, either
          in its visuals or in its functionality, as judged by a reasonable
          observer.

          Visual difference is judged at any time of day and in any
          weather, using the default settings of both packs. A Fork that
          only changes the appearance of a subset of times of day or weather
          conditions, and otherwise reproduces the appearance of the
          Original Pack, does not qualify on visual grounds. Difference
          achieved only by changing option values or presets does not
          qualify.

          Functional difference means the Fork adds, removes or changes
          features, settings or rendering behaviour in a way that is
          noticeable in use. Adding presets, or adding settings whose
          defaults reproduce the Original Pack, does not by itself qualify.

          A Fork whose only difference from the Original Pack is its name,
          its metadata, its packaging, or a cosmetic reorganisation of the
          code, such as renaming or reformatting, does not qualify under
          either heading.

       e. The Fork must be distributed solely under this license. It must
          not be accompanied by any other license, terms of service or
          condition, regardless of how much new code has been added. This
          does not prevent carrying the notices of third-party components
          that are already present in the Original Pack.

       f. This license file must be kept inside the Fork without
          substantive changes. Changes to line endings, character encoding,
          trailing whitespace or the file name do not count as changes.
          When the Fork is updated to make use of code from a newer version
          of the Original Pack, the license file must be replaced with the
          one found in that newer version.

       g. The Fork must not be sold, and must not be distributed in any way
          described in section 2.1, except that the Fork may be included in
          a Modpack on the terms of section 1.3. For that purpose, section
          1.3 is read with the Fork in place of The Pack, and condition 1.3.c
          requires only that the copy of the Fork placed in the Modpack be
          complete and unmodified.

  1.5. Unmodified copies of The Pack may be redistributed freely, including
       by uploading the files to another download page, as long as the
       following conditions are met:

       a. The copy is complete, includes this license file, and carries the
          same text of that file as the version being copied, apart from
          line endings, character encoding and trailing whitespace.

       b. kuwacom and the Original Pack are credited wherever the copy is
          offered, with a link to an Official Distribution Channel.

       c. The copy is not presented as the redistributor's own work, and is
          not presented as an official release of, or as endorsed by,
          kuwacom.

       d. Section 2.1 still applies. The copy must not be sold or placed
          behind any form of payment or advertisement gating.

       Section 1.3 applies instead of this section when The Pack is included
       in a Modpack.

  1.6. Users are free to read, examine and learn from the source code of
       The Pack. Implementing a technique, idea, algorithm, formula or
       visual approach found in The Pack in a different work is allowed and
       does not create a Fork. Copying code from The Pack into another work
       does create a Fork, and section 1.4 then applies to that work.

  1.7. Using The Pack, including its source code and generated assets, as
       training data for machine learning models is allowed.

  1.8. Any usage or redistribution not explicitly covered by this section
       is not granted and remains All Rights Reserved. The only exception
       is any file that carries a notice stating that it is covered by a
       different license, in which case that notice takes precedence.

2. Denied Cases

  2.1. The Pack and any Fork must not be sold, rented, sublicensed, or
       otherwise made available in exchange for money or any other
       consideration, except as permitted by section 1.3. This includes, but
       is not limited to:

       a. Paid downloads, donations-gated downloads, and downloads that
          require a paid membership.

       b. Paid early access, paid beta access, or subscriber-only tiers on
          platforms such as Patreon or Ko-fi.

       c. Distribution through advertisement-gated or shortened URLs, such
          as adfly and similar services.

       d. Inclusion in a paid support plan, paid installation service, or
          any product whose sale depends on The Pack or on a Fork.

  2.2. Extracting files or assets from The Pack and redistributing them on
       their own or as part of another work is not allowed. This includes
       textures, LUT data, generated noise images, lens data and isolated
       code snippets. Copying code into another shader pack is governed by
       section 1.6 instead. Such assets may appear incidentally inside
       screenshots, videos or renders made under Normal Usage, inside a copy
       of The Pack redistributed under section 1.5, and inside a Fork
       published under section 1.4.

  2.3. A Fork must not be relicensed, and must not be merged into a work
       that purports to license the Fork's code under different terms. This
       does not prevent the Fork from being included in a Modpack under
       section 1.3, where the Modpack's own terms apply only to the
       Modpack's own content.

  2.4. A Fork must not be presented as an official release of, or as
       endorsed by, kuwacom or the Original Pack.

3. Scope and Versioning

  3.1. This license applies only to the version of The Pack in which this
       license file is found. It does not apply to past or future versions
       of The Pack unless those versions contain a license file identical
       apart from line endings, character encoding and trailing whitespace.

  3.2. kuwacom may publish new versions of this license for future
       releases. Rights already granted for a published version are not
       revoked by a later version.

